from lib import *

slide("The proof, summed up", "The whole argument in one minute",
'''<ol class="prem" style="font-size:25px">
<li data-n="1">A price pays for the life a buyer expects.</li>
<li data-n="2">A maker who knows the product will give less, and says nothing, takes part of the price without consent. That is deceit, and the classical texts forbid it. <span class="tiny">(N1)</span></li>
<li data-n="3">The same choice harms the buyer and profits the maker, with no right behind it. <span class="tiny">(N2)</span></li>
<li data-n="4">What was sold is owned. Slowing, disabling or locking it from afar acts on another&#8217;s property. <span class="tiny">(N3)</span></li>
<li data-n="5">Only five defenses exist: no harm, consent, necessity, entitlement, others&#8217; benefit. Each fails, or only narrows the claim. The strongest, &#8220;it funds innovation,&#8221; fails five tests: it is hidden, a lawful route exists, the new product is either better or empty, it proves too much, and the payer is not the gainer.</li>
<li data-n="6">What stays lawful: an honest short life, support ended with notice, leases, restrictions the owner chose.</li>
<li class="concl" data-n="7">So: <b>tell the buyer, ask the owner, and leave him in charge.</b></li></ol>''')

slide("The proof, summed up", "What was shown, and how sure each step is",
'''<table class="tight" style="font-size:17px"><tr><th style="width:600px">Step</th><th>Basis</th><th style="width:190px">Mark</th></tr>
<tr><td>The map: four leaves, and what lies outside the claim</td><td>Yes/no splits; nothing can fall between branches</td><td>'''+chip("certain")+'''</td></tr>
<tr><td>N1 Consent: wealth passes only by informed consent; so concealing a known limit takes part of the price wrongly</td><td>Reason (price means something only if N1 holds); Qur&#8217;an 4:29</td><td>'''+chip("certain")+'''</td></tr>
<tr><td>A hidden limit on life is a concealed defect (<i class="t">tadlīs</i>)</td><td>Sound texts on deceit; analogy from the udder; Mecelle 67, 338</td><td>'''+chip("strong")+'''</td></tr>
<tr><td>N2 Harm: a choice that shortens life is harm without right</td><td>Reason; &#8220;no harm&#8221; hadith (disputed grades) and Mecelle 19&#8211;20</td><td>'''+chip("strong")+'''</td></tr>
<tr><td>N3 Ownership: remote control of a sold device needs informed permission</td><td>Mecelle 95&#8211;97, 100, 1192; the schools on conditions</td><td>'''+chip("strong")+'''</td></tr>
<tr><td>N4 Waste</td><td>Qur&#8217;an 17:26&#8211;27; hadith says <i>dislikes</i></td><td>'''+chip("support")+'''</td></tr>
<tr><td>Equivalence and gharar inside consent</td><td>Gabn rules (the strict school is met by deceit); Muslim 1513, fitted by our step</td><td>'''+chip("strong")+'''</td></tr>
<tr><td>Harm to many and to the earth</td><td>Mecelle 26, 27, 31, 87&#8211;88; Qur&#8217;an 7:56, 30:41; waste size not claimed</td><td>'''+chip("strong")+'''</td></tr>
<tr><td>The funding defense fails tests T1 to T5</td><td>Logic and Mecelle 22, 31, 33, 76, 87&#8211;88, 97; three hypotheses kept apart</td><td>'''+chip("strong")+'''</td></tr>
<tr><td>No defense survives: five places, all answered</td><td>The yes/no tree; each leaf answered</td><td>'''+chip("strong")+'''</td></tr>
<tr><td>Disclosed and chosen restrictions on repair (leaf C)</td><td>The schools differ; the narrow view adopted</td><td>'''+chip("probable")+'''</td></tr></table>
<p style="margin-top:16px"><b>The weakest link sets the mark.</b> The ruling as a whole is '''+chip("strong")+''', and in its core form, <i>concealing a known limit that sets the price</i>, it is '''+chip("certain")+'''.</p>''')

slide("The proof, summed up", "The price of rejecting the ruling",
'''<table style="font-size:20px"><tr><th style="width:560px">To reject the ruling you must&#8230;</th><th>&#8230;and then accept that</th></tr>
<tr><td><b>Deny that a buyer pays for what he expects</b> (step 1.1).</td><td>A price carries no information. No one could rationally pay in advance for anything.</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Deny that concealment removes consent</b> (N1).</td><td>Fraud in any sale is consensual, since every victim of fraud &#8220;agreed.&#8221;</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Deny that this is harm</b> (N2).</td><td>A seller may shift losses onto buyers whenever it pays him, if they are not told.</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Say the sold device stays the maker&#8217;s</b> (N3).</td><td>Then it was a lease. The price was rent, the word &#8220;sale&#8221; was false, and the buyer should have been told.</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Say the facts are absent in a given case</b> (F1&#8211;F3).</td><td>Then the case is outside the claim, and the claim agrees with you. You must show it.</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Say the maker needs the money for research.</b></td><td>Then he may say so and price openly (T1&#8211;T2). A model that is better needs no hidden failure; one that is not better funds nothing (T3).</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Accept a defense (D1&#8211;D5).</b></td><td>The answer already given to it, on the defense&#8217;s own slide.</td></tr></table>
<p class="small" style="margin-top:16px">So the ruling is not shielded by authority. It is open to anyone who can name a premise to give up, and the cost is shown beside each one.</p>''')

raw('''<section class="slide dark"><div class="kick" style="margin-top:36px">The ruling in force</div>
<h1 style="font-size:54px;line-height:1.14;margin-bottom:26px">What is forbidden, what is required, what is permitted</h1>
<div style="font-size:27px;line-height:1.45;max-width:1380px">
<p style="margin:0 0 14px 0"><b style="color:#7AD0C8">Forbidden.</b> To hide a limit on a product&#8217;s life or repair that the maker knows and the buyer does not. To slow, disable or lock a sold device, or to switch off a service it was promised, without the owner&#8217;s informed consent. To close the owner&#8217;s own means of repair beyond a narrow, stated safety need.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 14px 0"><b style="color:#7AD0C8">Required.</b> To tell the buyer the designed life and the support period where he can see them. To name what an update does when it costs a function, and to offer a real choice. To announce the end of support in good time and leave the device working.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 14px 0"><b style="color:#7AD0C8">Permitted.</b> Short-lived products honestly described. Budget and premium models together. Ending support with notice. Leases called leases. Updates under a general consent the owner can withdraw.</p>
<p style="margin:0"><b style="color:#7AD0C8">Remedy.</b> Rescission or compensation for the buyer, restoration where the device was changed, and <i>taʿzīr</i> by the ruler.</p></div>
<div style="position:absolute;left:92px;right:92px;bottom:22px;border-top:1px solid #3A4A5A;padding-top:8px;font-size:16px;color:#9FB1C2;display:flex;justify-content:space-between"><span>Planned Obsolescence</span><span>@N@</span></div></section>''')

slide("Limits of the claim", "What this talk does not claim",
'''<ul class="b" style="font-size:24px">
<li>That every short-lived product is wrongful. A short life that the buyer knows of is a lawful product.</li>
<li>That every maker intends harm. The ruling concerns the act: a known limit, hidden or imposed. Motive affects blame, not the duty to tell.</li>
<li>That products must be repairable by everyone, or supported forever. The ruling asks for notice, honesty and leaving the owner in charge.</li>
<li>That updates are forbidden. Updates are lawful under informed consent; only those that reduce a function need a specific one.</li>
<li>That a ban would raise or lower the rate of innovation, or that research budgets would grow by any amount. Those are hypotheses H1 to H3; the proof does not depend on them.</li>
<li>That planned obsolescence causes any stated share of the world&#8217;s e-waste. The size is unmeasured; only the direction is argued.</li>
<li>That fashion, advertising or taste are wrong. The claim concerns the device and the means of keeping it working.</li>
<li>That the four public cases prove the ruling. They test the map; they illustrate the tree. The ruling stands on the principles.</li>
<li>That any company is guilty today. Court and regulator records are cited as records, with their limits.</li></ul>''')

