slide("Glossary", "Terms used in this talk",
'''<table style="font-size:19.5px"><tr><th style="width:200px">Term</th><th>Meaning in this talk</th><th style="width:200px">Term</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>
<tr><td class="k"><i>ʿayb</i></td><td>A defect: what lowers the value of the goods in the eyes of the experts.</td><td class="k"><i>ʿilla</i></td><td>The cause or reason on which a ruling rests.</td></tr>
<tr><td class="k"><i>tadlīs, ghish, taghrīr</i></td><td>Deceit in a sale: hiding a defect, or showing a quality that is not there.</td><td class="k"><i>qiyās</i></td><td>Extending a ruling from a decided case to a new case that shares its cause.</td></tr>
<tr><td class="k"><i>khiyār al-ʿayb</i></td><td>The buyer&#8217;s option to rescind a sale because of a hidden defect.</td><td class="k"><i>ʿurf</i></td><td>Custom: what is settled and known in a trade.</td></tr>
<tr><td class="k"><i>taʿzīr</i></td><td>Discretionary punishment by the ruler.</td><td class="k"><i>mubāshir / mutasabbib</i></td><td>The direct actor / one who only causes the result (Mecelle 90&#8211;93).</td></tr>
<tr><td class="k"><i>ḍarar</i></td><td>Harm.</td><td class="k"><i>ijāra</i></td><td>Hire or lease: use for rent, without a transfer of ownership.</td></tr>
<tr><td class="k"><i>gharar</i></td><td>Uncertainty about what is sold: existence, amount or attribute.</td><td class="k"><i>gabn</i></td><td>Price disparity; <i>fâhiş</i> is gross, <i>yesîr</i> is small.</td></tr>
<tr><td class="k"><i>milk tāmm</i></td><td>Full ownership: of the thing and of its benefit.</td><td class="k"><i>iḍāʿat al-māl</i></td><td>Wasting wealth.</td></tr></table>''')
